# C1-S03 — A Normal Afternoon. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1626–1652.
# There's no alarm for about five minutes of play. The village has to feel lived
# in before anything threatens it. Each node is one NPC or moment; the
# farmers' argument sets up the uphill water in C1-S05, and the child sets up
# "Uncle Aldric" in C1-S08.
# rhythm: clipped old_fen old_fen_repeat
# (Old Fen speaks in as few words as he can get away with. That's him.)

~ chicken
Child: Mum! Mum, there's two Pebbles! The same one, twice, and they're both looking at me!
Mother: There's one Pebbles, love. There's always been one Pebbles.
do chicken_duplicate
Kaelen: ...
Kaelen: I'm not going to ask about the chicken. I've got a list, and it isn't on it.

~ old_fen
Old Fen: New, are you.
Kaelen: I guess so. Since about this morning.
Old Fen: You'll get over it.
Kaelen: Being new?
Old Fen: Guessing.

~ jessa
Jessa: So Elara brought you in, did she? You're bigger than her usual.
Kaelen: Her usual? Is this something she does a lot?
Jessa: She usually brings in plants. Sick ones, mostly. Nurses them back and gives them away.
Kaelen: Easier patients than me, I'd bet. They stay where you put them.
Jessa: And they wilt quieter. Plants don't ask where the crater went.

~ mara
Mara: So you're the crater. Sit down before you fall down. Have you eaten? Is she feeding you? Was it the stew again?
Kaelen: It was the stew. I had two bowls, and I'd have had a third if she'd looked away.
Mara: Course it was. It's always the stew. Here, end of the batch, still warm. Don't argue, I've already decided.
Kaelen: Thank you. I've got no money. I can fix things, mostly, if that's worth anything.
Mara: Thank me by not falling over in my doorway. We'll settle up when you've got money, and I'll remember the price.
set ch1_mara_met

~ farmers
Tull: Water doesn't go uphill, Wenna. It's water. It goes down. That's the whole of what it does.
Wenna: Then go and tell it that, because it's halfway up my bean rows.
Tull: You left the sluice open again, didn't you? I'm going to check either way.
Wenna: I've never left a sluice open in my life.
Tull: The spring of the flood. You left it open, and I said so at the time, and I've not changed my mind.
Wenna: That was the sluice's fault.

~ lost_sword
Child: Have you seen my sword? It's wood. It's the best one in Oakhaven, because it's the only one.
Kaelen: I haven't, sorry. What does it look like?
Child: Like a sword. A wooden one.
Kaelen: ...I walked into that. I'll look under things. Lost things are always under things.

~ lost_sword_found_pickup
Kaelen (Internal): A wooden sword, half under a bush. It's a good one, too. Someone carved the grip.

~ lost_sword_found
Child: You found it! I knew somebody would! Are you a knight? You've got a sword, so you might be.
Kaelen: No. I've got the sword, but mostly I look like I lost a fight with one.
Child: My uncle Aldric's a knight. A proper one. He's away right now, but he's coming back soon, so you can meet him.
set ch1_child_sword_returned

# ── Second visits: everyone has something, nobody goes silent ─────────────

~ lost_sword_waiting
Child: I was playing by the south fence, near the field path, so it's there. Or it's somewhere else. Probably there.

~ child_repeat
Child: I'm going to show Uncle Aldric the sword the second he's back. He'll say it's a good one, because it is.

~ farmers_repeat
[if not ch1_north_field_helped] Tull: Still uphill. I've checked it twice and I'm going to check it again.
[if not ch1_north_field_helped] Wenna: He's been checking it all morning, love. The beans don't care who's right. They're drowning.
[if ch1_north_field_helped] Wenna: Water's going downhill again. Tull's terribly upset about being right.
[if ch1_north_field_helped] Tull: I'm not upset. I'm vindicated. It's a different feeling.

~ wenna_repeat
Wenna: Don't take sides in this, love. It's between me, Tull and that sluice, and the sluice started it.

~ old_fen_repeat
Old Fen: Still new.

~ jessa_repeat
Jessa: If Elara ever hands you a plant, water it and leave it be. Same goes for her.

~ mother_repeat
Mother: One Pebbles. I counted this morning. I count every morning now.

# ── Free roam: repeat visits, the shop, the market stone, Bran's post ─────

~ mara_repeat
Mara: Back again? Hungry? Got your hands free? Buy something or carry something, love. Pick one.

~ whispering_stone
Kaelen: What is this thing? It's humming, and I'm fairly sure rocks don't.
Elara: The Whispering Stone. It tells you prices, mostly.
Kaelen (Internal): Numbers crawling up a rock. Grain in Ironhold, iron in places I've never heard of. It's a live market feed, carved into stone.
Kaelen: Does anybody actually use it?
Elara: Rook does, when he comes through. Everyone else just argues with it.
set ch1_auction_house_visited

~ whispering_stone_repeat
Kaelen (Internal): Bread's up two coppers since this morning. Mara will have something to say about that.

~ bran_repeat_field
Bran: North field first. There's no field mud on those boots yet, so don't tell me you've been. Then we'll talk roads.

~ bran_repeat_road
Bran: The bridge is south, lad. Have a good look before you trust your weight to it, and come back and tell me what you saw.

# Data Vision secret under Bran's gatepost.
~ guard_post_secret
System: TRACE: EVACUATION_RIGHTS.CLAUSE — DISABLED.
Kaelen (Internal): Someone switched off a rule about leaving. A long time ago. Right under Bran's gatepost.

~ elara_repeat
Elara: Go on, have a look around. Light's good till supper. I'll be here, pretending I'm not watching you.
